# The oracle references, pinned.
#
# One line per reference, tab-separated: <name> <image> <version> <what it
# answers>. Machine-read by tools/oracle/oracle_env.py.
#
# Built here: no upstream digest of the finished image. What is pinned is
# everything the Containerfile reads, and the run-time version check is the
# guarantee. Raising a pin is deliberate - a newer Argyll or littleCMS is
# newer answers.
#
# Building them:
#   make oracle-build
# which builds every image named below.

# ArgyllCMS 3.3.0 (Debian). Lookups go through icclu (icclib V3.1.0 bundled
# in the package): it accepts the CMYK and RGB v2 LUT fixtures this library
# generates. xicclu 3.3.0 is also present and is what names the package
# version in the probe. Neither tool in this package supports ICC v4, so the
# mAB fixture is outside this oracle's reach - stated, not hidden. That is
# why littleCMS is pinned beside it.
argyll	localhost/ghoti-color-oracle-argyll:3.3.0	Lookup ICC or CAL colors, Version 3.3.0	ICC matrix/TRC and v2 LUT (mft1/mft2) device→PCS lookups via icclu; independent CMM reading beside littleCMS

# littleCMS 2.16 (Debian). Lookups go through lcms_icc_lookup (built into the
# image against liblcms2). This is the CMM that can judge ICC v4 mAB /
# parametricCurveType fixtures Argyll refuses. Not linked into the library —
# independence from lcms2 stays structural; the gate compares two programs.
lcms2	localhost/ghoti-color-oracle-lcms2:2.16	LittleCMS 2.16	ICC matrix/TRC, v2 LUT, and v4 mAB device→PCS lookups via liblcms2

# libtiff 4.7.0 (Debian). The SGI LogLuv reference: libtiff's SGILog codec is
# Larson's own. logluv_vectors (built into the image) writes codes and reads
# floats, and the reverse; tools/oracle/gen_logluv.py turns its answers into
# tests/data/logluv/ and src/math/logluv_uv_table.h. Asked only when the
# vectors are regenerated - make test reads the committed answers.
libtiff	localhost/ghoti-color-oracle-libtiff:4.7.0	libtiff 4.7.0	LogL16, LogLuv24 and LogLuv32 decode and encode via libtiff's SGILog codec
